{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "ethan.brooks", "message": "Heads up: NorthBay Manufacturing pushed their onboarding kickoff to next Wednesday due to an ERP cutover. Commercially we’re still targeting a 10/1 go-live for the Dallas warehouse + LTL lane coverage. I’ll update the forecast notes so Finance isn’t surprised by the slip.", "create_at": 1764948000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "ops-execution", "channel": "sla-credits-and-reporting", "user": "lucas.nguyen", "message": "For the Q2 SLA credit report, we’re seeing inconsistent timestamps from the Toronto facility scans (some are logging in local time, some UTC). Ops analytics is fixing the ETL, but until then the on-time % is underreporting by ~1.5–2 pts. Please hold off on sharing external performance summaries for Toronto lanes until we re-run the dashboard.", "create_at": 1764948600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "redline-summary-rss14", "user": "maria.chen", "message": "Quick housekeeping: I renamed the RSS-14 tabs to match the new customer naming convention ("CustomerName_Country_YYYYMM"). If you have bookmarks to the old tab names, they’ll need to be refreshed. Also added a column for "Doc version received" so we can track when customers send multiple marked copies.", "create_at": 1764949200000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "priya.desai", "message": "Reminder that Legal is doing mandatory training on the updated data retention policy this Friday at 11:00am CT (30 min). The main change is how we store customer shipment-level data in shared drives vs. the contract repository—IT will cover the practical do’s/don’ts.", "create_at": 1764949800000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "ops-execution", "channel": "sla-credits-and-reporting", "user": "lucas.nguyen", "message": "Customer feedback item: three shippers flagged that our weekly performance PDFs are too dense. Proposal is to lead with a 1-page executive summary (late shipments, root causes, corrective actions) and move the lane-level detail to an appendix. If Sales wants to pilot with two accounts, I can draft the new format by Monday.", "create_at": 1764950400000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "redline-summary-rss14", "user": "ethan.brooks", "message": "On a separate note, I’m at the CSCMP regional event next week. If anyone wants me to sit in on specific sessions (nearshoring trends, 2026 LTL capacity outlook), drop topics here and I’ll take notes for the team.", "create_at": 1764951000000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "redline-summary-rss14", "user": "ethan.brooks", "message": "Heads up: Apex Components just sent a new round of redlines and wants signature by EOW. What’s the fastest path to get these approved internally without 10 back-and-forth emails?", "create_at": 1775364600000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "redline-summary-rss14", "user": "maria.chen", "message": "Fastest way is to drive everything through the Redline Summary Sheet (RSS-14). I’m preparing it now.

Process we use to approve redlines quickly:
1) I extract each customer deviation (by clause) into RSS-14.
2) For each deviation, Legal proposes (a) our preferred response and (b) fallback language we can live with.
3) We tag the business/risk owner for any residual risk (e.g., Finance for liability cap exceptions, Ops for SLA/service credit mechanics) and get their explicit sign-off in the sheet.
4) Once RSS-14 is complete, we post it in #deal-approvals for a single-thread decision instead of multiple reviewers re-reading the full redline.
5) After owners approve the residual risk + fallback positions, Priya can confirm we’re within guardrails and we move to signature-ready docs.

This reduces cycle time because approvers can decide off the deltas + named risk owner, not re-litigate the whole agreement.", "create_at": 1775364900000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "redline-summary-rss14", "user": "priya.desai", "message": "Yep. If RSS-14 clearly shows (1) what changed, (2) our fallback, and (3) who is accepting the residual risk, I can usually turn legal approval same-day.

Key is: don’t wait for a “perfect” redline. Capture the deltas in RSS-14 first, then we resolve only the true exceptions. Anything within our standard guardrails gets a quick “OK” and we focus on the outliers.", "create_at": 1775365080000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "maria.chen", "message": "Posting RSS-14 draft for Apex Components here shortly. Heads-up: they added SLA service credits + monthly reporting requirements, plus a tweak to the credit cap.

Once we approve/sign, we need to hand off the exact SLA credit obligations (triggers, calculation, cap, and reporting timelines) to Ops so they can track credits and reporting on day 1. If we don’t capture it post-signature, we risk missing the reporting window and auto-credits.", "create_at": 1775365260000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "ethan.brooks", "message": "Thanks. For approvals: what do you need from me specifically—just confirm commercial impact of the service credits + any pricing offsets?", "create_at": 1775365380000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "priya.desai", "message": "From Sales (you):
- Confirm the commercial rationale for the SLA service credit terms (and whether any concessions are tied to it).
- Confirm you’re aligned with the fallback position Maria lists (so we don’t reopen negotiation internally).

From our side, we’ll route to the right risk owner(s) in RSS-14. Once each owner signs off on residual risk, I’ll mark “Legal Approved” and Maria can finalize signature packet.", "create_at": 1775365500000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "ops-execution", "channel": "sla-credits-and-reporting", "user": "lucas.nguyen", "message": "Looping in based on Maria’s note: if the Apex contract includes SLA service credits + monthly reporting, please send us the executed SLA exhibit and the final credit language (triggers, exclusions, cap, and reporting due dates).

Post-signature we’ll:
1) Create the SLA credit tracker entry (customer + site lanes).
2) Assign an ops owner for credit calculation/approval.
3) Set calendar reminders for reporting timelines.
4) Confirm system fields (WMS/TMS notes) so execution teams can flag incidents.

This handoff is what prevents compliance misses even when Legal turns approvals quickly.", "create_at": 1775365740000}}
{"type": "post", "post": {"team": "commercial-legal", "channel": "deal-approvals", "user": "maria.chen", "message": "Perfect—this is exactly why we call out SLA credits in RSS-14 and then do an ops capture immediately after signature. I’ll attach the final executed SLA exhibit here and also drop it in #sla-credits-and-reporting once signed.", "create_at": 1775365920000}}
